  "origin": {
   "confidence": "medium"
  },
  "rationale": "\"Fast. Private. No distractions.\" is three short phrases that each stand alone. The Korean puts a full stop after word forms that need something to follow them: \"빠르고\" and \"보호되고\" end in \"-고\" (\"and…\"), and \"없는\" needs a noun after it. A noun-style ending (빠름 / 사생활 보호 / 방해 없음) keeps the three short phrases and is grammatical.",
  "reads_as_deliberate": false,
  "resolved_on": "",
  "status": "open",
  "string_hash": "3c53d16e",
  "string_id": "onboarding_first_screen_subtitle",
  "suggest": "빠름. 사생활 보호. 방해 없음.",
  "summary": "The subtitle ends sentences with full stops after a connective (-고) and a modifier (-는), so it reads as ungrammatical Korean.",
  "suppressed_by": ""
 },
